01:32.820 --> 01:36.020
Brazil - Sao Paulo suburbs

01:50.240 --> 01:53.620
It's my seventh game with Brancos since I made the first team.

01:58.050 --> 02:02.170
Your opponent today, Domingo's Carlos Santana,

02:02.170 --> 02:07.850
has strength unmatched by anyone you've faced so far.

02:08.640 --> 02:12.900
He's known as "the Son of the Soccer God."

02:27.650 --> 02:30.940
Another great day. Thank you, God.

02:30.940 --> 02:33.030
Time for work.

02:48.170 --> 02:50.540
How can this be? It's a baby!

03:08.020 --> 03:09.310
Oh, God!

03:18.010 --> 03:22.890
The Soccer God must have sent him to me.

03:28.580 --> 03:32.160
The Son of the Soccer God, Santana.

03:37.240 --> 03:42.380
<b>The Soccer Cyborg {TLC:  Was this the title for ep 33 at the end of ep 32?  I can't remember since I worked on ep 32 so long ago.  I'm asking because I can't check myself.  Don't have ep 32 on this computer.}</b>

03:37.240 --> 03:42.380
<b>The Soccer Cyborg {TLC:  Was this the title for ep 33 at the end of ep 32?  I can't remember since I worked on ep 32 so long ago.  I'm asking because I can't check myself.  Don't have ep 32 on this computer.}</b>

03:56.840 --> 04:01.180
Be wary of the Brancos' Tsubasa Ohzora. We're playing against him today.

04:01.180 --> 04:05.960
He's got eight assists and five goals so far this season.

04:05.960 --> 04:08.500
Don't underestimate him just because he's Japanese.

04:09.440 --> 04:14.020
People in Japan call him "the kid born to play soccer." {koku@Kaiser's note: yes he said 申し子 or "heaven-sent child" if you want the direct TL, but this term has also been routinely translated as "high flyer" "[fill in the blank, eg internet] darling" or "child of the [eg: theater]"}

04:16.020 --> 04:19.740
Nelson and Marissi, tightly mark Ohzora in this game.

04:20.370 --> 04:22.130
Stay right on him.

04:22.130 --> 04:25.160
Leo, you're not in the starting lineup today,

04:25.160 --> 04:28.060
but depending on the situation, you may be subbed in to support Santana.

04:28.060 --> 04:28.740
Got it?

04:28.740 --> 04:30.260
Yes!

04:35.120 --> 04:35.780
Santana.

04:37.580 --> 04:39.780
We can't lose this game.

04:42.190 --> 04:47.840
Oh, that's right. It doesn't matter who you're up against.

04:49.940 --> 04:52.240
I will just play soccer with the ball.

04:55.630 --> 04:59.030
We're counting on you again, Son of the Soccer God.

05:08.390 --> 05:12.340
No matter who we're playing against, I'm Brancos' number 10.

05:12.340 --> 05:14.770
I'll play soccer worthy of my number.

05:17.620 --> 05:20.140
I vow it before my misanga!

05:20.950 --> 05:24.280
You're still wearing the misanga I gave you?

05:26.120 --> 05:29.330
Even though I don't know what your wish is.

05:29.330 --> 05:31.700
Enough with the small talk, Pepe.

05:35.280 --> 05:36.880
Leandro.

05:36.880 --> 05:40.600
Pepe, Tsubasa is preparing for the game.

05:40.600 --> 05:42.890
A reserve player shouldn't be disturbing him.

05:42.890 --> 05:43.860
Fine.

05:45.500 --> 05:47.860
Tsubasa, we're counting on you today, too.

05:47.860 --> 05:48.900
Yes!

05:49.670 --> 05:54.800
I think I could contribute more to the team if I started in his place!

05:54.800 --> 05:55.560
What?

05:55.560 --> 05:56.360
Pepe!

05:56.740 --> 05:58.460
I can hear you.

06:01.520 --> 06:03.710
Good night, Mom.

06:03.710 --> 06:05.850
Okay, good night.

06:12.920 --> 06:14.400
Tsubasa-kun...

06:17.970 --> 06:22.500
God, Soccer God, if you really exist,

06:22.500 --> 06:26.770
please watch over Tsubasa-kun so he doesn't get injured.

06:28.580 --> 06:32.900
Brazil - Santa Familia Stadium

06:46.780 --> 06:48.530
This atmosphere...

06:48.530 --> 06:51.180
I just can't get enough of being on the pitch!

06:55.010 --> 06:58.140
Tsubasa sure is calm.

06:58.140 --> 06:59.820
That's it, Tsubasa.

06:59.820 --> 07:02.380
Don't get flustered by Santana's soccer.

07:02.380 --> 07:04.980
You just play your own soccer.

07:08.380 --> 07:11.600
The match between the Brancos and Domingo is about to start!

07:11.600 --> 07:13.810
The center of attention is definitely these two.

07:13.810 --> 07:15.720
Branco's young number 10,

07:15.720 --> 07:19.940
Tsubasa Ohzora, who's flourishing as the playmaker of the team.

07:22.180 --> 07:27.340
And Domingo's number 10, Santana, is said to be the crown jewel of Brazilian soccer.

07:27.830 --> 07:31.500
These two young athletes will play against each other for the very first time!

07:31.500 --> 07:33.330
What a loud crowd!

07:33.330 --> 07:34.090
Yes, you're right.

07:34.090 --> 07:36.450
However, no matter how well Tsubasa plays,

07:36.450 --> 07:41.020
it will be difficult to beat the Son of the Soccer God, Santana.

07:41.660 --> 07:43.150
Santana...

07:43.790 --> 07:48.030
"Legend has it that he's the Son of the Soccer God."

07:49.660 --> 07:51.340
Did you hear about this? "The Son of the Soccer God."

07:52.850 --> 07:56.970
Well, Santana's skills may be godly,

07:56.970 --> 07:59.380
but I hate the way he plays soccer.

07:59.380 --> 08:01.120
Why?

08:01.120 --> 08:03.340
There's not a hint of joy when he scores.

08:03.820 --> 08:08.470
He doesn't have passion like us.

08:09.390 --> 08:11.010
The Son of God, huh?

08:13.220 --> 08:16.380
Santana, what are you looking at?

08:19.380 --> 08:23.380
Santana's eyes aren't on us; he only sees the ball!

08:28.840 --> 08:32.380
Brancos vs Domingo, kick off!

08:32.580 --> 08:35.860
Oh! Tsubasa is dribbling a straight line through Domingo territory!

08:35.860 --> 08:37.510
What a bold move.

08:37.510 --> 08:40.700
He doesn't seem to be nervous playing against them for the first time.

08:41.970 --> 08:45.700
This entire pitch is my backyard!

09:00.980 --> 09:04.020
Santana, why aren't you moving?

09:14.300 --> 09:16.820
He's dribbling the ball as if it's stuck to his cleats!

09:17.850 --> 09:19.560
He evades another!

09:19.560 --> 09:22.900
Tsubasa easily dodges the Domingo defense!

09:29.380 --> 09:34.380
Santana is not moving, but his eyes are locked on the ball!

09:34.380 --> 09:36.300
Damn, I'm stopping you!

09:38.150 --> 09:40.780
If Santana refuses to move...

09:42.030 --> 09:44.020
Tsubasa brilliantly maneuvers past the fourth player!

09:44.020 --> 09:46.180
I'll seize this chance!

09:47.740 --> 09:50.400
He passes to the side towards Giorgino!

09:50.400 --> 09:53.300
The ball is moving too fast! Is it heading out?

09:53.300 --> 09:55.640
No! There's huge spin on the ball!

09:55.640 --> 09:58.300
As usual, Tsubasa's passes are easy to handle!

10:00.940 --> 10:03.420
Leandro is running toward Giorgino's pass!

10:03.420 --> 10:04.660
This is a great chance for the Brancos!

10:05.660 --> 10:06.980
I got it!

10:06.980 --> 10:08.700
I won't let you score!

10:08.700 --> 10:09.860
I'll stop him!

10:13.960 --> 10:15.860
A desperate save by Domingo!

10:15.860 --> 10:17.700
Brancos fails to score!

10:17.700 --> 10:20.340
Ah... so close.

10:20.340 --> 10:21.460
It's not over yet.

10:21.980 --> 10:24.060
But the ball is still in play!

10:24.700 --> 10:25.420
Oh!

10:26.840 --> 10:29.300
Tsubasa is heading towards the ball!

10:31.760 --> 10:33.500
Tsubasa! Go for it!

10:34.060 --> 10:36.380
A Domingo defender is closing in!

10:49.460 --> 10:50.540
Go in!

10:51.380 --> 10:54.660
He scores! Goal!

10:54.660 --> 10:57.100
Brancos scores first!

10:55.210 --> 10:56.290
{stack}Good job!

10:56.290 --> 10:59.740
He did it! He scored already!

10:59.740 --> 11:01.060
Yes!

11:01.490 --> 11:03.580
It's almost as if he knew the ball would drop there.

11:03.580 --> 11:05.580
He scored with a spectacular Overhead Kick!

11:05.580 --> 11:07.580
Tsubasa Ohzora of the Brancos!

11:14.070 --> 11:18.780
Here's an interview with Branco's number 10, Tsubasa Ohzora, the scorer of that goal.

11:18.780 --> 11:22.090
Great play, Tsubasa! Nice goal!

11:22.090 --> 11:24.220
Is it all right if I interview you?

11:24.220 --> 11:25.790
Sure!

11:25.790 --> 11:30.300
The surprise attack right after the whistle and your dribbling were magnificent!

11:30.300 --> 11:34.330
You have total control of the ball, as if it's your servant.

11:34.340 --> 11:34.860
What?

11:34.860 --> 11:38.860
No. The ball isn't my servant.

11:38.860 --> 11:42.700
The soccer ball is my precious friend!

11:42.700 --> 11:45.680
I see. The ball is your friend!

11:45.680 --> 11:47.570
That's the comment from Tsubasa Ohzora!

11:49.150 --> 11:50.940
The ball is his friend...

11:59.280 --> 12:05.340
The Brancos fans are chanting "Tsubasa" because he scored the first goal!

12:05.860 --> 12:10.150
On the other hand, Domingo's supporters are chanting Santana's name.

12:11.000 --> 12:15.650
Being one point down, fans are cheering in hopes of him tying the game!

12:17.150 --> 12:20.970
Santana has drawn the attention of all Brazilian soccer fans.

12:20.970 --> 12:27.290
Santana, the Son of the Soccer God, is surely the next in the line of Brazillian superstars

12:27.290 --> 12:32.380
who will wear the number 10 jersey in the next International Cup.

12:55.020 --> 12:55.780
He's fast!

12:55.780 --> 12:58.300
Santana breaks through the midfield with his dribble!

12:58.300 --> 13:01.670
Tsubasa awaits him in his path!

13:01.670 --> 13:03.380
Come, Santana!

13:05.790 --> 13:07.430
A head-on battle!

13:10.430 --> 13:14.440
Oh! Santana turns around in front of Tsubasa!

13:16.250 --> 13:20.100
I-I can't see the ball!

13:20.880 --> 13:23.220
What's wrong? Did you lose the sight of your friend?

13:31.620 --> 13:34.100
Can you believe it? The ball passed over Tsubasa's head!

13:34.660 --> 13:36.580
The ball is a part of my body.

13:41.140 --> 13:43.970
Tsubasa is completely beaten!

13:43.970 --> 13:46.140
This is the Santana Turn!

13:46.140 --> 13:47.980
Tsubasa! Get back!

13:49.140 --> 13:52.630
Santana leaves Tsubasa behind!

13:55.200 --> 13:57.580
The Soccer Cyborg has been activated.

14:00.980 --> 14:01.660
I'll stop him!

14:06.540 --> 14:07.580
Is he passing?

14:11.940 --> 14:15.200
Great play! He feints a pass and then runs past a defender again!

14:15.200 --> 14:15.820
Damn!

14:17.740 --> 14:18.860
He runs past another!

14:18.860 --> 14:21.490
How far can Santana get by himself?

14:20.870 --> 14:22.020
Oh no you don't!

14:22.020 --> 14:23.260
Yeah!

14:23.260 --> 14:27.770
Three defenders from the Brancos are charging at him! This is a raging defense!

14:29.330 --> 14:31.380
They stopped Santana!

14:33.020 --> 14:33.820
I'm not losing the ball.

14:35.200 --> 14:35.820
What?!

14:36.280 --> 14:39.270
Amazing! Incredible tenacity with the ball!

14:39.270 --> 14:41.940
And incredible technique!

14:41.940 --> 14:42.940
What?

14:42.940 --> 14:44.100
I'm not going to let you score!

15:01.140 --> 15:02.400
Right there!

15:13.430 --> 15:15.900
Goal! Goal!

15:15.900 --> 15:18.540
Santana! Santana! Santana!

15:19.060 --> 15:21.060
1-1!

15:21.060 --> 15:23.520
Domingo ties the game!

15:26.060 --> 15:27.580
He's got us!

15:28.170 --> 15:31.220
His Rolling Overhead Kick is godly, indeed.

15:31.220 --> 15:35.230
He took intense tackles, but his uniform is still spotless!

15:35.230 --> 15:38.140
It's tied in no time!

15:39.820 --> 15:41.300
Incredible!

15:41.300 --> 15:45.010
There's a storm of chanting in the stadium!

15:46.100 --> 15:48.530
What a show, Santana!

15:48.530 --> 15:49.990
We've been waiting for this!

15:52.050 --> 15:53.570
Uh, um...

16:00.480 --> 16:02.480
The Son of God, Santana.

16:02.480 --> 16:05.580
Every single move of his was precise and powerful.

16:05.580 --> 16:09.580
But... why is he so cold?

16:09.820 --> 16:11.660
The game resumes.

16:21.650 --> 16:25.030
Brancos vs Domingo, an even match!

16:25.030 --> 16:28.390
The game is at a standstill, tied 1-1.

16:33.830 --> 16:37.980
Tsubasa and Santana are both tightly marked and can't move!

16:44.680 --> 16:48.780
The Brancos vs Domingo game has entered stoppage time.

16:48.780 --> 16:52.060
It seems the first half will end with a tie.

16:58.650 --> 17:01.610
The ball is passed to Giorgino! No one's marking him!

17:01.610 --> 17:02.140
Tsubasa!

17:04.900 --> 17:06.490
Go!

17:09.060 --> 17:09.900
Good play!

17:09.900 --> 17:13.620
Tsubasa escaped from the defenders and receives the pass!

17:14.170 --> 17:15.260
Oh, no!

17:15.260 --> 17:17.750
Tsubasa runs straight to the goal!

17:18.260 --> 17:19.060
Oh!

17:20.060 --> 17:23.060
The person standing in his way is...

17:23.060 --> 17:24.420
Santana!

17:24.420 --> 17:25.820
Santana's there!

17:26.050 --> 17:27.820
Santana, let's do this!

17:30.580 --> 17:31.540
Huh?

17:31.540 --> 17:32.340
What?

17:32.340 --> 17:36.980
Tsubasa is doing a Santana Turn!

17:36.980 --> 17:39.740
The ball passes over Santana's head!

17:39.740 --> 17:42.750
He's already mastered the Santana Turn?

17:42.750 --> 17:44.140
You really are something...

17:48.540 --> 17:50.660
Santana launches an Overhead Kick!

17:50.660 --> 17:52.860
I see! So that's how you counter it!

17:53.520 --> 17:55.700
Giorgino regains possession of the ball!

17:55.300 --> 17:56.620
Take the ball!

17:56.620 --> 17:58.340
The pass goes to Leandro!

17:58.340 --> 18:00.660
There's no time! Go, Tsubasa!

18:01.100 --> 18:01.900
He passes forward!

18:02.560 --> 18:04.340
It's headed for Tsubasa!

18:04.340 --> 18:06.980
Tsubasa is running toward the goal!

18:07.480 --> 18:09.900
Soccer is not played alone.

18:09.900 --> 18:13.980
No matter how much you cover me, the team can't be stopped!

18:14.500 --> 18:17.260
A clean pass to Tsubasa!

18:17.260 --> 18:19.500
But there's not enough time!

18:20.050 --> 18:23.060
Oh? Santana has stopped again.

18:23.550 --> 18:25.310
The referee is checking his watch.

18:24.580 --> 18:27.140
Hurry, Tsubasa! There's no time!

18:27.140 --> 18:29.210
Block his shooting path!

18:29.210 --> 18:29.660
Right!

18:30.850 --> 18:33.700
Domingo defenders are blocking the shooting path!

18:36.020 --> 18:37.100
Go!

18:39.610 --> 18:42.950
Is it too high?

18:42.950 --> 18:44.260
No, this is...

18:44.260 --> 18:45.220
What?!

18:45.220 --> 18:48.270
Goal! It's in!

18:48.270 --> 18:50.850
Tsubasa scores again!

18:50.850 --> 18:52.570
Two goals by Tsubasa!

18:52.570 --> 18:56.030
Yes, yes, yes!

18:57.860 --> 19:02.500
Tsubasa's shot just now... the ball spun differently and fell.

19:02.500 --> 19:06.050
Unlike the normal Drive Shoot that only rotates vertically,

19:06.610 --> 19:10.010
this Drive Shot utilizes multi-directional spins,

19:10.010 --> 19:13.340
allowing Tsubasa to curve the ball any way he wants.

19:14.500 --> 19:18.540
Tsubasa has perfected the Flying Drive Shot!

19:18.540 --> 19:21.800
I'm surprised he pulled it off in this situation.

19:21.800 --> 19:24.020
Impressive, Tsubasa!

19:25.360 --> 19:28.460
The first half is over!

19:28.460 --> 19:32.610
Brancos leads Domingo again, 2-1!

19:34.990 --> 19:37.580
Two spectacular goals, Tsubasa!

19:37.580 --> 19:39.620
The fans are ecstatic!

19:40.400 --> 19:41.980
Thank you.

19:41.980 --> 19:47.230
You're wearing three misangas. What's your wish?

19:47.230 --> 19:52.060
The first is to play this season without injury.

19:52.060 --> 19:56.300
The second is for the Brancos to be number one in Brazil.

19:56.300 --> 19:58.740
And the third...

19:58.740 --> 20:04.300
Is my wish for the Japanese team to win the next International Cup!

20:06.080 --> 20:08.690
You have ambitious dreams!

20:08.690 --> 20:10.300
Good luck in the second half!

20:10.300 --> 20:16.260
Thanks! I'll make my dreams come true - for the fans, too!

20:17.750 --> 20:18.840
Prayer?

20:19.450 --> 20:20.500
Wishes?

20:21.330 --> 20:22.310
Dreams?

20:24.830 --> 20:26.790
How can you let this happen?

20:26.790 --> 20:29.050
We're down by one!

20:29.050 --> 20:34.910
Aren't you guys ashamed of letting a young Japanese kid run circles around you?

20:37.360 --> 20:39.460
Just pass the ball to me.

20:42.160 --> 20:44.890
His age and nationality are meaningless.

20:45.540 --> 20:47.380
So are prayers and wishes.

20:48.870 --> 20:50.920
The strong will win.

20:51.420 --> 20:53.550
That's what soccer is all about.

20:58.140 --> 21:01.970
If you want to win, pass the ball to me.

21:05.010 --> 21:08.390
Santana! The meeting is not over yet!

21:08.390 --> 21:10.570
We will win this game.

21:12.980 --> 21:16.000
What's with his attitude?

21:16.000 --> 21:19.190
Is he trying to say that it's our fault we're losing?

21:19.190 --> 21:20.980
"Pass the ball to me"?

21:56.780 --> 21:58.660
For me, soccer is...

22:00.250 --> 22:01.630
Destiny.

22:04.020 --> 22:10.660
Preview

22:05.820 --> 22:07.620
It's the seventh game for the Brancos.

22:07.620 --> 22:11.330
Carlos Santana stands in our way on the pitch.

22:11.330 --> 22:16.500
His cyborg-like precise and powerful dribbling rips across the pitch,

22:16.500 --> 22:19.490
but his eyes are cold and lonely.

22:19.490 --> 22:24.570
Santana, what do you see from your sorrowful eyes?

22:24.570 --> 22:26.190
Next time, on Captain Tsubasa:

22:25.300 --> 22:34.100
The Son of God, Santana

22:26.190 --> 22:27.340
The Son of God, Santana.

22:27.340 --> 22:28.730
Look forward to it!

22:28.610 --> 22:30.960


22:28.730 --> 22:31.570
Let's aim for tomorrow! Get goal!

22:37.860 --> 22:44.860
<b>Keep on going mirai ga mieta toki ni</b>

22:37.860 --> 22:44.860
<b>Keep on going, when you saw the future {"Keep on going. When you see the future,}</b>

22:37.860 --> 22:44.860
<b>Keep on going, when you saw the future</b>

22:44.860 --> 22:51.060
<b>arifureta hibi ga kagayakidasu yo</b>

22:44.860 --> 22:51.060
<b>those mundane days are shining forth {Are we not putting punctuation on the ends of lines?}</b>

22:44.860 --> 22:51.060
<b>those mundane days are shining forth</b>

22:51.060 --> 23:04.020
<b>kodou ga hazumu jikan wo kimi to tomo ni hashirou</b>

22:51.060 --> 23:04.020
<b>Our hearts are racing, so let's run together</b>

22:51.060 --> 23:04.020
<b>Our hearts are racing, so let's run together</b>

23:04.020 --> 23:10.700
<b>tsuyokina kaze wo kokoro ni unerasete</b>

23:04.020 --> 23:10.700
